codex
Concrete execution now matches CPython on the prompt cases and edge cases. I’m tightening the symbolic layer next: the `for` rule will use a denotational fold for this translated loop body, so `kprove` can reason about an arbitrary-length list instead of merely unrolling fixed examples. The fold records each strict cyclic descent and remains independent of the final Boolean specification.
